Changes from the upstream work
------------------------------

Text Adventure is not the upstream product. It is a derivative that keeps the
upstream runtime and replaces the surrounding product with a single-purpose
narrative game. The principal changes are:

- The product surface is reduced to one activity: playing and authoring
  interactive text-adventure stories. Product areas unrelated to that activity
  were removed rather than hidden.
- Branding, interface copy and the desktop entry point are renamed to
  Text Adventure (TA), and the default data root is `.ta-game`.
- Game systems were extended: character attributes and cultivation progress,
  item and equipment handling with per-grade identity, combat rounds, world
  clock and deadlines, faction and organisation affairs, spirit beasts,
  character messaging, and intimacy/relationship flows.
- Story-pack authoring was extended with the world, character, location,
  faction and rule structures the game systems consume.
- A local package updater (`TA-updater`) replaces updating from the upstream
  release channel. This build refuses to update from the upstream channel by
  design, because the upstream channel publishes a different product.
- Third-party notices for the compiled distribution are collected under
  `licenses/third-party/` at packaging time.

Files that carry the upstream copyright notice are not individually marked;
this NOTICE and the modification history in the source repository identify the
work as changed.

